<title>COLOMBIA: Bavaria most active Colombia stock in 1H.</title>
<headline>Bavaria most active Colombia stock in 1H.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brewing giant Bavaria was Colombia's most actively traded stock in the first half of this year, the Securities Superintendency said Thursday.</p>
<p>The stocks watchdog awarded Bavaria an index of 8.77 -- calculated on the number of trades and volume traded.</p>
<p>Second placed was Banco de Colombia, the country's second largest bank in terms of assets, with an index of 8.44.</p>
<p>Cement manufacturer Cemento Argos, part of the powerful Sindicato Antioqueno industrial conglomerate, with an 8.13 index was the third most actively traded stock on Colombia's Bogota, Medellin and tiny Cali-based exchanges.</p>
<p>Supermarket chain Cadenalco with an index of 8.05 was the only other stock to score higher than eight.</p>
<p>((--Juan Guillermo Londono, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944))</p>
